# Known bug: casting a copy of a split card from Uldaros Theorix always uses way 0 (cast_during_resolution), the card as a whole, so no half is chosen and the copy resolves as a token permanent "Life // Death" (CR 709.3, 709.3a, 601.2); the half cast should be chosen and its mana value counted.
# Uldaros Theorix and a split card (CR 709.3): a copy of Life // Death is cast as one half, the player's choice, and the spell on the stack
# has only that half's characteristics, so what counts towards the six is that half's mana value - Death's 2 or Life's 1, not
# the 3 the two halves make in exile. Bot1 Entombs Life // Death and a creature (Ornithopter) and exiles them with the Lotus; it
# casts the Death copy, which returns the Ornithopter card from the graveyard (the Death copy targets it).

